Adam Silva Consulting puts a 64 rack AI cluster over 10 years at $42 million on advanced

00:09:57.467 --> 00:10:03.047
air, $31 million on direct-to-chip liquid, and $28 million on single-phase immersion.

00:10:03.707 --> 00:10:06.307
Air down to the tank is a $14 million gap.

00:10:06.927 --> 00:10:09.207
Direct-to-chip down to the tank is $3 million.

00:10:09.767 --> 00:10:14.307
The bath wins the 10-year cooling spend, and it wins by less against the liquid design

00:10:14.307 --> 00:10:15.347
that keeps the cabinet.

00:10:15.347 --> 00:10:21.507
A $350,000 premium per megawatt has to come back out of that $3 million edge.

00:10:21.887 --> 00:10:24.447
Plus any floor space and energy the bath saves.

00:10:25.067 --> 00:10:30.327
The source never turns those 64 racks into megawatts, so there is no payback year to quote.

00:10:30.847 --> 00:10:33.347
The comparison that is printed is already the problem.

00:10:33.947 --> 00:10:35.747
Operations do the rest of the blocking.

00:10:36.347 --> 00:10:41.067
Once airflow is not the constraint, row pitch and white space can change, and the article

00:10:41.067 --> 00:10:41.867
