00:10:41.867 --> 00:10:47.547
A technician lifts a board out of a tank, not out of a cabinet, monitoring, service steps,

00:10:47.767 --> 00:10:49.387
and training move with that change.

00:10:49.807 --> 00:10:54.487
Direct to chip still asks for new plumbing, but it leaves more of the rack habit intact,

00:10:54.987 --> 00:10:57.047
which is why a hull can adopt it in pieces.

00:10:57.667 --> 00:11:03.127
The tank stops losing to the $650,000 install when heat density and water limits make a

00:11:03.127 --> 00:11:09.647
$3 million 10-year edge on that $64 rack cluster, and a $14 million edge against advanced

00:11:09.647 --> 00:11:12.867
air, worth redrawing the room and retraining the floor.

00:11:13.567 --> 00:11:15.467
Data center knowledge's test is plain.

00:11:16.047 --> 00:11:20.067
If training and inference keep getting hotter, and if the pressure to cut water and energy

00:11:20.067 --> 00:11:22.927
rises with them, the bath gets harder to refuse.

00:11:23.547 --> 00:11:28.267
If that build out flatens before the capital and the crew change, immersion remains what

00:11:28.267 --> 00:11:29.587
it is in 2026.

